## 8. Cross-cutting rules

- Settings: every threshold, limit, cap or retention window is an admin-editable setting with a seeded default
  (`docs/templates/settings-entry.md`), never a code literal.
- Migrations: expand / contract (`docs/templates/migration-file.md`), applied by CI, never from a laptop.
{%- if multi_tenant %}
- Tenancy: every tenant table has row-level security with FORCE; tenant queries run only through
  `TenantScopedPool.transaction(tenant_id)` (`api/app/tenancy.py`), which sets the tenant per transaction. A tenant
  holds at most `jobs.max_running_per_tenant` running jobs (fair-share gate).
{%- endif %}
{%- if ai_features %}
- AI: every model call goes through the gateway (`api/app/gateway.py`: routes by role, fallback, monthly spend caps
  checked before the call) and is written to the call ledger with its billed tokens and cost (`docs/ai/README.md`).
{%- endif %}

